<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aranuka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aranuka is a small atoll in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-islands">Gilbert Islands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiribati">Kiribati</a>, near Abemama, made up of two main islets around a lagoon. In the 19th century the rulers of Abemama, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tem-baiteke">Tem Baiteke</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tem-binoka">Tem Binoka</a>, brought it under their kingdom, which was absorbed into the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> Islands in 1892.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aranuka.jpg" alt="Aranuka" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of USA, Government of Kiribati · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:10_Map_of_Aranuka,_Kiribati.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
